  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef alphago_l01_resolve_move(board: list, action: list, player: int, consecutive_passes: int = 0) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Apply a legal stone placement or pass action to a Go board, resolve any resulting stone captures, and update player turns and terminal game states.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nApply a legal stone placement or pass action to a Go board, resolve any resulting stone captures, and update player turns and terminal game states.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef alphago_l01_resolve_move(board: list, action: list, player: int, consecutive_passes: int = 0) -> dict:\n    b = np.array(board, dtype=int).copy()\n    H, W = b.shape\n    opponent = 3 - player\n    if action is None or len(action) == 0:\n        new_passes = consecutive_passes + 1\n        return {'board': b.tolist(), 'next_player': opponent, 'consecutive_passes': new_passes, 'captures': 0, 'is_terminal': new_passes >= 2}\n    r, c = action[0], action[1]\n    b[r, c] = player\n    captures = 0\n    for dr, dc in [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]:\n        nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n        if 0 <= nr < H and 0 <= nc < W and b[nr, nc] == opponent:\n            v, q, grp, has_lib = set([(nr, nc)]), [(nr, nc)], [], False\n            while q:\n                curr_r, curr_c = q.pop(0)\n                grp.append((curr_r, curr_c))\n                for d1, d2 in [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]:\n                    ar, ac = curr_r + d1, curr_c + d2\n                    if 0 <= ar < H and 0 <= ac < W:\n                        if b[ar, ac] == 0:\n                            has_lib = True\n                        elif b[ar, ac] == opponent and (ar, ac) not in v:\n                            v.add((ar, ac))\n                            q.append((ar, ac))\n            if not has_lib:\n                for gr, gc in grp:\n                    if b[gr, gc] == opponent:\n                        b[gr, gc] = 0\n                        captures += 1\n    return {'board': b.tolist(), 'next_player': opponent, 'consecutive_passes': 0, 'captures': captures, 'is_terminal': False}\n```\n\n### 📊 Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where operations scale linearly with input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for output buffers and intermediate tensors.\n\n### 🔍 How It Works\n1. **Input Normalization & Setup:** Validates data structures and initializes buffers.\n2. **Core Transformation:** Executes the mathematical logic adhering strictly to numerical standards.\n3. **Robust Handling:** Manages boundary conditions, edge cases, and numerical stability.\n",
